{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Aptos;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green119\blue182;}\paperw11906\paperh16838\margl1134\margr1134\margt1134\margb1134 \pard\cf1\b\fs36 Qilly BOQ Unit Rules and Pricing Calculations\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Implementation reference - active production code reviewed 14 September 2026\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 1. Active calculation sequence\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Ordinary material amount = total landed cost x CIDB factor x duration factor x machinery factor x (1 + profit margin).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Base price: supplier catalogue rate, adjusted by selected-province factor and transport optimisation.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab CIDB: GB1 +2%; GB2 +3%; GB3 +4%; GB4 +5%; GB5 +6%; GB6 +7%; GB7 +8%; GB8 +9%; GB9 +10%. Unknown classes default to +5%.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Duration: 1 month +5%; 2-3 months +2%; 4-12 months 0%; 13-18 months -1%; 19-24 months -2%; 25-36 months -3%.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Machinery: owned -5%; rented +3%.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Profit: applied last; selectable from 1%-25%.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Final unit rate = final amount / BOQ quantity. Adjustments compound.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 2. Quantity rules\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Valid numeric QTY multiplies ordinary material, labour and equipment rates.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Blank or zero QTY returns zero pricing for ordinary items.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Invalid text QTY falls back to 1 in several paths; stricter validation is recommended.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Rate Only in the QTY column is converted to QTY 1 and marked rate-only.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Lump, prime-cost and provisional sums are forced to QTY 1.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Square-metre totals now correctly use landed rate x QTY; the prior one-unit defect was fixed.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 3. Special units\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab PROVISIONAL SUM aliases: provisional sum, p/s, prov sum, or description containing provisional sum. Catalogue/provincial price is used directly; QTY 1; no CIDB, duration, machinery or user margin.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab PRIME COST SUM aliases: prime cost, pc sum, pc, or description containing prime cost/pc sum. Catalogue/provincial price + fixed 12.5% handling; QTY 1; no other project adjustments.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab LUMP SUM aliases: lump sum, lumpsum, lump, ls, l/s, sum. Catalogue/provincial price + fixed 5% coordination overhead; QTY 1; no other project adjustments.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab PERCENTAGE aliases: % or text containing percent. Active engine treats these as special but does not reliably calculate against a referenced BOQ item.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab NO MATCH: unmatched special items currently receive a R50,000 placeholder and Not Available supplier status. This must not be relied on for tender submission.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 4. Ordinary unit families and aliases\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Bag: bag, bags (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Count: unit, units, ea, each (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Number: No/no and nr work as ordinary units with QTY multiplication but are not centrally normalised.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Length: meter, meters, metre, metres, m (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Area: m2, m squared, sqm, squaremeter, square meter, square metre (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Hectare: ha, hectare, hectares; 1 ha = 10,000 m2.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Volume: m3, cubicmeter, cubic meter (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Tonnes: ton, tons, tonne, tonnes, t, mt, metric ton, metric tons.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Kilograms: kg, kgs, kilogram, kilograms; legacy tonne relationship uses factor 1,000.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Litres: liter, litre, l, ltr, liters, litres (1:1).\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Millilitres: ml and full-name variants; 0.001 litre.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Kilolitres: kl and full-name variants; 1,000 litres.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Month: ordinary unit; amount uses the month QTY.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Percentage: %, percentage, percent.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab The conversion families are in the legacy engine. The active regional engine mainly trusts supplier catalogue totals and does not consistently invoke this conversion table.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 5. Proposed BOQ comparison\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Fixed/value obligations - lump sum: supported; QTY 1; fixed 5% overhead.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Mobilisation - month x 3: supported.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Execution - month x 8: supported.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab De-establishment/re-establishment - No x 1: supported as ordinary units.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Suspension - month x 4: supported.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Engineer's cost - prime cost (PC) sum: supported; QTY 1; fixed 12.5% handling.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Contract sign boards - m2 x 20: supported and corrected to scale by 20.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab TOTAL CARRIED FORWARD TO SUMMARY: row is preserved, but active regional engine currently returns zero instead of summing the section.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 6. Province and project settings\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Project pricing is available for all nine South African provinces regardless of a contractor's registered operating provinces.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Operating provinces can be updated on the dashboard.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Project duration includes every integer month from 1 through 36.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 7. Known gaps and recommended rules\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab HIGH: replace the R50,000 special-sum fallback with a required tender-entered rate/amount or Pricing Required.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab HIGH: imported RATE and AMT columns are detected but not retained in the BillItem model; add tenderRate and tenderAmount.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab HIGH: calculate TOTAL CARRIED FORWARD using explicit parent/child codes or a declared range.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab MEDIUM: require a reference code for percentage rows and calculate QTY% x referenced amount / 100.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab MEDIUM: centralise unit normalisation across upload, categorisation and both engines.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab MEDIUM: test kilogram/tonne conversion direction and rate semantics.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab LOW: remove duplicate special-unit detection to prevent alias and markup drift.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 8. Recommended canonical units\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab No.; item; sum; lump sum; prime cost (PC) sum; provisional sum; %; month; hour; day; m; m2; m3; km; kg; t; L; kL; bag; pair; set.\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Aliases may be accepted during upload but should be normalised to these display values.\par \par \pard\cf1\b\fs28 Document status\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\li240\fi-180\bullet\tab Describes Qilly code deployed on 14 September 2026. Special-sum commercial treatment is documented, not redesigned. Handling-percentage changes require approval.\par \par }